\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Effect size.}
The pairwise $r^2 \approx 1.3\text{--}1.7\%$ is modest but concentrates among pairs the model actually confuses ($\rho = 0.27\text{--}0.31$; \S\ref{sec:pairwise}). At the batch level, BCS-controlled accuracy gaps reach 31.2\,pp and amplify $3.4\times$ from 16 to 80 relations---a small pairwise signal compounding into large effects when confusable types co-occur.

